  "body": "## What changed\n\nSix shape tests now run in three independent integration targets.\nThe batch scheduler can run these targets beside the motion lib target.\nThe remaining 16 tests stay in the original unit module.\nAll 22 tests, the existing ignore marker, and all 61 original assertion lines remain.\n\nSmaller passing fixtures reduce repeated work.\nThe shared quality helper uses a D/60 debug grid.\nRelease checks keep the D/80 grid.\nThe wide-pocket test has a 90-second execution budget.\nThe decision file records the fixture choices and rejected alternatives.\n\nSeven expensive tests shared the motion lib target.\nParallel batch lanes could not finish before that target.\nFixture changes alone reduced the local lib time by only 7.7 percent.\nThe target split removes that scheduling limit without a production API change.\n\n## Review fix\n\nMerge head: `cea210c817eae3bc8e0b2e56f237910ea4b8df43`.\nMerged upstream main: `f85163b0c`.\n\nThe merge resolves the conflicts in `crates/app/tests/pocket3d_hsm.rs`.\nThat file now matches upstream main exactly.\nIt keeps the Linux x86_64, Windows x86_64, and macOS aarch64 count pins and their exact-count tests.\nThe mesh, cutting-level, verification, fallback, and planning-budget assertions remain.\n\n## Validation on the merge head\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: PASS. All 179 steps passed in 21.1 minutes. There were 1,900 passes, zero failures, and 71 ignored tests.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: PASS.\n- App `pocket3d_hsm` debug suite: PASS. Two tests passed and two were ignored.\n- Release test `the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean`, with `--ignored --exact`: PASS. One test passed in 1.88 seconds.\n- Linux pin mutation: RED, then GREEN. The old tuple `(4726, 4698, 549)` failed the assertion at line 224 with exit 101. Restoring the file bytes made the exact pin pass with exit 0.\n\nThe Linux pin test is `the_linux_x86_64_bore_count_pin_is_exact`.\nThe full bore test checks the mesh, cutting levels, counts, and safety assertions.\nThe conflict file matches upstream main exactly.\nThe tracked tree is clean.\n\n## Earlier measurements\n\nThese measurements precede the merge head.\nTheir base was `58cb641caa0a4c0b6d514c3e874ccaee1b8a6e5b`.\n\nThe timing pin is `adaptive_troch_parallel::wide_rectangular_pocket_is_cleared_by_parallel_lanes`.\nThe initial pin failed on unchanged fixtures after 178.44 seconds.\nThe final budget is 90 seconds, with margin for concurrent tests.\n\nThe earlier mutation restored the upstream 60x40 fixtures and D/80 measurement helper.\nThe geometry assertions passed.\nThe timing assertion failed after 122.38 seconds.\nRestoring the fix made the same pin pass in 40.26 seconds.\n\nThe six moved tests keep their confinement, crossing, engagement, slotting, and residual-area checks.\nTheir test count remains six.\nThe unit module keeps the other 16 tests.\nThe existing ignored L-shape test remains ignored.\n\n| Target | Before | After |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| Motion lib | 207.11 s | 62.51 s |\n| `adaptive_troch_parallel` | part of lib | 40 s |\n| `adaptive_troch_island` | part of lib | 109 s |\n| `adaptive_troch_neck` | part of lib | 111 s |\n\nThe original lib run had 486 passes, one timing-pin failure, and 10 ignored tests.\nThe earlier final lib run had 482 passes and nine ignored tests.\nThe new targets retained the other five passes and one ignored test.\nThe lib also passed with two test threads in 131.33 seconds.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\nThe NC and CL diff against upstream main is empty.\n\n## Not exercised on the merge head\n\nThe post-merge runner was not used.\nThe issue's 567-second runner baseline and these local measurements use different environments.\nThe full batch, heavy, and release tiers were not run on the merge head.\nThe ignored L-shape test was not run on the merge head.\nWindows and macOS were not exercised.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #2990\n",
